---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/about`;
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    "@id": `${url}#aboutpage`,
    url,
    name: "About Thomas McKee, Design Engineer, Edinburgh",
    isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
    about: { "@id": `${SITE}/#thomas-mckee` },
    mainEntity: { "@id": `${SITE}/#thomas-mckee` },
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": `${SITE}/#thomas-mckee`,
    name: "Thomas McKee",
    jobTitle: "Design Engineering Consultant",
    description: "Design engineer with over four years developing award-winning consumer products at Ooni, spanning mechanical design, firmware and thermal engineering. Now an independent product development consultant in Edinburgh.",
    url,
    worksFor: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    alumniOf: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Ooni" },
    homeLocation: { "@type": "Place", address: { "@type": "PostalAddress", addressLocality: "Edinburgh", addressCountry: "GB" } },
    knowsAbout: [
      "Design engineering",
      "Consumer product development",
      "Mechanical design",
      "Firmware",
      "Thermal analysis",
      "Design for manufacture",
      "Prototyping",
      "Injection moulding",
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "About", item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="About, Thomas McKee, Design Engineer in Edinburgh | Ex-Ooni"
  description="Thomas McKee is a design engineering and product development consultant in Edinburgh with 4+ years shipping award-winning consumer hardware at Ooni, mechanical, firmware and thermal, from concept to volume manufacture."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap svc-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">About · Thomas McKee</span>
        <h1>A bit <em>about me</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">I'm a design engineer based in Edinburgh. For over four years at Ooni I took premium consumer products from first concept to volume manufacture, and now I do the same as an independent partner to founders and startups building physical products for the first time.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Work with me <span class="arw">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#services">See services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="Profile">
        <div class="spec-head"><span>Profile</span><span>TMDE-001</span></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Engineer</div><div class="spec-v">Thomas McKee</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Discipline</div><div class="spec-v">Design Engineering</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Based</div><div class="spec-v">Edinburgh, UK</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Prev.</div><div class="spec-v">4+ yrs · Ooni</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Scope</div><div class="spec-v">Mech · Firmware · Thermal · DFM</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Status</div><div class="spec-v">Available for projects</div></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">The background</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">From mechanical engineer to firmware lead</h2>
      <div class="about-body" style="max-width:70ch">
        <p>I trained and started out as a mechanical engineer, but consumer products don't respect the neat boundaries between disciplines, so I didn't either. On the Ooni Volt 2, an electric indoor pizza oven, I ended up as the firmware lead despite the mechanical background, because that's what the product needed and I was willing to learn it. I owned the performance and control system end to end: the thermal behaviour, the heating hardware, and the firmware that ties them together.</p>
        <p>That pattern, following a product wherever the hard problem is, rather than staying in a lane, is the thing I've come to trust most about how I work. It means I see mechanical, firmware, thermal and manufacture as one system, and I can spot the rare moments where a single decision improves time, cost <em>and</em> performance together, instead of trading one against another.</p>
        <p>Across four years at Ooni I took products from the first sketch through to volume manufacture, worked on the factory floor where they were built, and helped bring several award-winning consumer products to market. Today I bring that whole-picture experience to founders and startups as Thomas McKee Design Engineering.</p>
        <p>It's worth being clear about what kind of help this is. I'm a design engineer, so my job is making a product actually work and actually be manufacturable. That's a different discipline from industrial design, which is about how a product looks and feels, and different again from a design studio that lists "design for manufacture" next to its styling work. When your product needs the aesthetic side, I bring in industrial designers I trust rather than stretching past what I do best. What you get from me is the engineering that decides whether a product survives tooling, volume and real use, grounded in having done exactly that on the factory floor.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I BRING -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">What I bring</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">The things clients say matter most</h2>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3>The whole picture</h3><p>Mechanical, firmware, thermal and manufacture seen as one system, so decisions are made with every consequence in view, and the occasional "unicorn moment" where everything improves at once actually gets caught.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3>Structure &amp; rhythm</h3><p>Most of my clients are doing this for the first time. What helps most is a steady, honest process, walking through the real development journey, then a clear plan with fast, fail-fast prototyping that keeps momentum without losing the essence of the idea.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3>Plain-English engineering</h3><p>The decisions, the trade-offs and the occasional physically impossible spec, explained clearly, whoever I'm working with. You always understand where your product is and why.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CAPABILITY -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Capability</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Skills, software and processes</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">The full toolkit I bring to a project. The case studies show most of it in action, and this is the rest of what I can take on.</p>
      <div class="caps">
        <div class="capcol">
          <div class="cap-h">Core skills</div>
          <div class="cap-tags">
            <span class="tag">Mechanical design</span>
            <span class="tag">FEA</span>
            <span class="tag">Structural analysis</span>
            <span class="tag">Hand calculation</span>
            <span class="tag">Mathematical modelling</span>
            <span class="tag">Tolerance stack analysis</span>
            <span class="tag">GD&amp;T</span>
            <span class="tag">CFD</span>
            <span class="tag">Thermal engineering</span>
            <span class="tag">DFM &amp; DFA</span>
            <span class="tag">Tooling development</span>
            <span class="tag">Requirements &amp; verification</span>
            <span class="tag">Materials selection</span>
            <span class="tag">Supplier liaison</span>
            <span class="tag">Industrial design intent</span>
            <span class="tag">Application firmware</span>
            <span class="tag">Control systems &amp; state machines</span>
            <span class="tag">Combustion &amp; airflow</span>
            <span class="tag">Test rig design &amp; instrumentation</span>
            <span class="tag">Standards compliance &amp; certification</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="capcol">
          <div class="cap-h">Software &amp; tools</div>
          <div class="cap-tags">
            <span class="tag">SolidWorks &amp; PDM</span>
            <span class="tag">SolidWorks Simulation</span>
            <span class="tag">SolidWorks Flow Simulation</span>
            <span class="tag">ANSYS Mechanical</span>
            <span class="tag">MATLAB</span>
            <span class="tag">Python</span>
            <span class="tag">KeyShot</span>
            <span class="tag">Multi-channel data logging</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="capcol">
          <div class="cap-h">Manufacturing processes</div>
          <div class="cap-tags">
            <span class="tag">Injection moulding</span>
            <span class="tag">Pressure die casting</span>
            <span class="tag">Sheet metal stamping &amp; pressing</span>
            <span class="tag">Deep drawing</span>
            <span class="tag">CNC machining</span>
            <span class="tag">Laser cutting</span>
            <span class="tag">Welding</span>
            <span class="tag">Powder coating</span>
            <span class="tag">Soft tooling &amp; rapid prototyping</span>
            <span class="tag">High-volume assembly</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRACK RECORD -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Track record</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Shipped, recognised, and sold worldwide</h2>
      <div class="proof">
        <div class="pl">The work</div>
        <p>My work has reached the shelf and been recognised for it: the Ooni Volt 2 won a <a href="https://www.red-dot.org/project/ooni-volt-2-85947" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--ember)"><strong>Red Dot Design Award in 2026</strong></a>, with the citation calling out the performance functions I led; the Ooni Karu 2 won an <a href="https://ifdesign.com/en/winner-ranking/project/ooni-karu-12g-multi-fuel-pizza-oven/643103" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--ember)"><strong>iF Design Award</strong></a> and a <strong>German Design Award in 2024</strong>, and its door architecture was carried onto the <a href="https://ifdesign.com/en/winner-ranking/project/ooni-karu-2-pro/709204" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--ember)">iF-winning Karu 2 Pro in 2025</a>. I'm named on <strong>three patented or patent-pending inventions</strong>, and my products are sold worldwide. The through-line isn't the awards, though, it's that these were hard products that had to work, be safe, be manufacturable and be loved, all at once.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci"><b>Red Dot 2026</b> · Ooni Volt 2</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>iF &amp; German Design Award 2024</b> · Ooni Karu 2</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>3 patented or patent-pending</b> · Red Dot &amp; iF Design Awards · sold worldwide</span>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="/#work" style="color:var(--ember)">See the case studies →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VALUES -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">What I stand for</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">How I choose to work</h2>
      <div class="values" aria-label="Values" style="margin-top:8px">
        <div class="val"><div class="vh"><span class="n">01</span> Integrity</div><div class="vd">Decisions are evidence based and transparent, with clear communication on where trade-offs need to be made.</div></div>
        <div class="val"><div class="vh"><span class="n">02</span> Thoughtful Innovation</div><div class="vd">Creative solutions to practical engineering problems that aren't complex for the sake of complexity.</div></div>
        <div class="val"><div class="vh"><span class="n">03</span> Long-Term Solutions</div><div class="vd">In both design and process, ensuring early work is done properly to reduce the risk of re-work.</div></div>
        <div class="val"><div class="vh"><span class="n">04</span> Positive Impact</div><div class="vd">Engineering should be a force for good, used meaningfully whether in a commercial or pro-bono setting.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRO BONO -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Beyond the commercial</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Engineering that gives something back</h2>
      <div class="about-body" style="max-width:70ch">
        <p>Alongside client work, I dedicate part of my time to <strong>pro-bono engineering</strong> for initiatives with social or environmental impact. I believe good engineering should contribute beyond commercial success, so by working with me, you help support that too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="band alt" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Let's talk</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Have a product that needs to become real?</h2>
          <p>Tell me where you are and where you're stuck. Whether it's a first concept or a design that needs to survive manufacturing, I'll tell you honestly how I can help.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Or start with a <b>£50 Power Hour</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<style>
  .caps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,40px);margin-top:30px}
  .capcol .cap-h{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ember);padding-bottom:11px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:16px}
  .cap-tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}
  .cap-tags .tag{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-2);background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:6px;padding:6px 11px;line-height:1.2}
  @media (max-width:820px){.caps{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:26px}}
</style>
</Base>
